WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:09.800
Here's how to sign in with Google the first time. You link your Google account once, and after that, your volunteer page opens with one tap.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:15.400
Step one. On the Hub's volunteer page, tap Sign in with Google.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:23.540
Step two. Pick your Google account. Any Google account works. It doesn't have to be the email the Hub sends to.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:29.895
Step three. If the Hub already has your Google email, your page just opens, and you're done.

00:00:30.095 --> 00:00:35.740
If not, you'll see this welcome screen. Already volunteering? Use the bottom box.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:44.036
Step four. Enter the volunteer code from any Hub email. It looks like four letters and numbers, a dash, and four more.

00:00:44.236 --> 00:00:48.360
Then tap Link my Google account. You only do this once.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:55.110
Step five. Don't have your code? Tap, Email it to me. It's right under the Link button.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:01:01.123
Step six. Enter the email your Hub emails come to, and tap Email my code.

00:01:01.323 --> 00:01:08.330
Your code, and a button that opens your page, arrive in a minute or two. Then come back and enter the code.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:16.980
Step seven. You're in! From now on, Sign in with Google opens your page with one tap, on any phone or computer.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:26.620
Step eight. One heads up. Once you link Google, typing just your email won't open your page anymore. Use Sign in with Google, or your code.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:32.890
Family members on the same email can use the same Google account, or their own code.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:38.680
Questions? Email the IU liaison from the bottom of any Hub page.
